<title>SPAIN: Spain approves telecoms bill to liberalise sector.</title>
<headline>Spain approves telecoms bill to liberalise sector.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's cabinet approved on Friday a telecoms bill that will pave the way for the liberalisation of its telecommunications sector, Development Minister Rafael Arias Salgado said.</p>
<p>&quot;The cabinet approved the telecoms bill that will regulate a liberalised sector and the provision of telephone services,&quot; the minister told a news conference after the cabinet's weekly meeting.</p>
<p>The bill must now be passed through Congress.</p>
<p>Spain, in agreement with the European Union, plans to fully liberalise its telecoms sector by the end of November 1998.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
</text>
